lowrate for DN200/DN250\"\n- \"5\", 17 April 2025, \"Addition of the reduced bore version with ratio 400 and software version 2.0.60\"\n- \"6\", 31 July 2025, \"Addition of horizontal housing, IP68 variant and software version 2.0.61\"\n- \"7\", 3 October 2025, \"M5000 Facelift - upgrade of electronics housing and external battery version. Addition software version 2.0.62\"\n- \"8\", 3 October 2025, \"Textual adjustments\"\n- \"9\", 23 December 2025, \"Evaluation of remote mount version and software update\"\n- \"10\", 5 March 2026, \"Manufacturer name change and documentation folder update\"\n- \"11\", 28 July 2026, \"Software update and checksum correction\"\n\nSchema: revision (string, e.g. \"0\" not 0), date, changes. \"Initial\" → \"0\". Dates: ISO format \"2021-01-11\" etc.\n\n**Recommendation:** R49 — the fragment doesn't state \"OIML R 2013\" explicitly but the number \"R49/2013-A-NL1-21.03\" contains R49 and edition year 2013. Recommendation id: \"R49\", edition: 2013, scheme: \"A\". Accuracy classes: not present.\n\nThe number format: R49/2013-A-NL1-21.03. R49 = recommendation, 2013 = edition year of the recommendation, A = scheme, NL1 = issuer, 21.03 = certificate serial. So recommendation: {id: \"R49\", edition: 2013, scheme: \"A\"}.\n\n**certificate:**\n- number: \"R49/2013-A-NL1-21.03\"\n- scheme: \"A\"\n- project_number: \"4141724\"\n- page_total: 7\n- member_state: \"The Netherlands\"\n- date_issued: \"2026-07-28\" (revision 11 date — current revision). Include? The fragment supports it via revision history. I'll include it.\n- oiml_issuer_id: \"NL1\"\n\n**issuing_authority:**\n- name: \"NMi\"\n- oiml_issuer_id: \"NL1\"\n\n**test_reports:** none in fragment. Omit.\n\n**characteristics.type_level:** nothing whole-cert that isn't model-dependent here. The software versions are approved across all models — could be type_level list? Not a single value though. Skip.\n\n**components:** Possibly the indicating device? Table 4 is \"General characteristics of