nly.\n\nHmm, on reflection, I'll skip components to avoid half-baked structures. The matrix_tables with clear names carry the info.\n\n**matrix_tables:**\n\n1. Table 4 — General characteristics of the indicating device:\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"General characteristics of the indicating device\",\n  \"columns\": [\"meter_size\", \"indicating_range\", \"verification_scale_interval\"],\n  \"column_units\": [null, \"m³\", \"m³\"],\n  \"rows\": [\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN50\", \"indicating_range\": 99999, \"verification_scale_interval\": 0.0001},\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN65; DN80; DN100; DN125\", \"indicating_range\": 999999, \"verification_scale_interval\": 0.001},\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN150\", \"indicating_range\": 999999, \"verification_scale_interval\": 0.01},\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN200 till DN350\", \"indicating_range\": 9999999, \"verification_scale_interval\": 0.01},\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN400 till DN500\", \"indicating_range\": 9999999, \"verification_scale_interval\": 0.1},\n    {\"meter_size\": \"DN600\", \"indicating_range\": 99999999, \"verification_scale_interval\": 0.1, \"footnotes\": [\"*\"]}\n  ],\n  \"description\": \"Indicating range and verification scale interval per meter size. Values with dots are thousands separators as printed (e.g. 9.999.999 = 9 999 999).\",\n  \"footnotes\": [\"* This display indication range is only available with software revision 2.0.52 or later...\"]\n}\n```\n\nWait — the footnotes[] in matrix_tables: should it be full text or markers? Schema says footnotes[]. I'll put the full text or the marker. The global footnotes[] has marker+text objects. For matrix_tables footnotes, I'll list marker \"*\" or the text. I'll use the marker \"*\" and rely on global footnotes for text. Hmm, example shows footnotes[] in matrix_tables without defined shape. I'll put the marker string.\n\nActually, maybe row-level footnote marker: rows entry \"footnote_markers\": [\"*\"]. I'll add that to the DN600 row.\n\n2. Table 5 — Approved 