entioned.\n\nFinal: use group conditions as in table. In matrix_tables rows they're preserved anyway.\n\nHmm, actually let me reconsider once more. \"DN200 till DN350\" — in these NMi certificates for Itron water meters (this looks like an Itron cert — project 4141724, software versions 2.0.x, M5000... actually M5000 is an Itron water meter family name, yes Itron M5000... actually Itron has \"Gallonmeter\"... whatever). DN sizes between DN200 and DN350: DN250, DN300. The Q4 correction for \"DN200/DN250\" in rev 4 strongly suggests DN250 is a listed size. DN300 likely too. But strictly, I keep groups.\n\n**characteristics.model_level:**\n\nattribute: indicating_range\n- unit m³\n- values: per model row as above with footnote on DN600.\n\nattribute: verification_scale_interval\n- unit m³\n- values per row.\n\nI'll write:\n\n```json\n\"model_level\": [\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"indicating_range\",\n    \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"model\": \"DN50\", \"value\": 99999},\n      {\"model\": \"DN65; DN80; DN100; DN125\", \"value\": 999999},\n      {\"model\": \"DN150\", \"value\": 999999},\n      {\"model\": \"DN200 till DN350\", \"value\": 9999999},\n      {\"model\": \"DN400 till DN500\", \"value\": 9999999},\n      {\"model\": \"DN600\", \"value\": 99999999, \"footnote_markers\": [\"*\"]}\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"verification_scale_interval\",\n    \"unit_symbol\": \"m³\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"model\": \"DN50\", \"value\": 0.0001},\n      {\"model\": \"DN65; DN80; DN100; DN125\", \"value\": 0.001},\n      {\"model\": \"DN150\", \"value\": 0.01},\n      {\"model\": \"DN200 till DN350\", \"value\": 0.01},\n      {\"model\": \"DN400 till DN500\", \"value\": 0.1},\n      {\"model\": \"DN600\", \"value\": 0.1}\n    ]\n  }\n]\n```\n\nPer rule 2, every characteristic value MUST be an object with value/unit_symbol/unit_id/footnote_markers. The R137 example shows model_level values as {\"model\": \"G1.6\", \"value\": 2.5} without unit_symbol... The example in rule 4 shows {\"model\": \"G1.6\", \"value\": 2.5}. But rule 2 says strict object shape. The R137 example is abbreviated. I'll follow the R137 example shape (model+value) at the value-entry level, since unit_symbol is on the attribute level. The schema says:\n\n```\nmodel_level[]:\n  attribute, unit, values[]: {model, value, footnote_markers[]}\n```\n\nOK so schema says values[]: {model, value, footnote_markers[]}. Good — I'll follow that.\n\n**Footnotes global:**\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"marker\": \"*\",\n    \"text\": \"This display indication range is only available with software revision 2.0.52 or later, other software versions shall not be used for meter size DN600. Additionally, this display indication range is only available with standard cover, IP68 cover shall not be used for meter size DN600.\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\n**certified_type:**\n```json\n{\n  \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n  \"type_designations\": [\"M5000\"]\n}\n```\n\nHmm, category — should I? The fragment never says \"water meter\". R49 = \"Water meters\" — well-known. The certificate number starts with R49. I'll include \"Water meter\". Alternatively omit category. I'll include it; it's derivable and low-risk.\n\ntype_designations: \"M5000\" from rev 7. Include.\n\n**certificate.date_issued**: \"2026-07-28\" — the date of revision 11 which is the current revision. Include.\n\nNow the software matrix table rows — merge pages 5 and 6 (same table, columns identical). Yes.\n\nRemarks column: \"-\" for first row, empty for others. I'll omit empty remarks or set null. For first row, remarks \"-\". I'll include remarks: \"-\" for row 1 and omit/null for others. To keep JSON clean, include \"remarks\": null? Or just \"-\". I'll use \"-\".\n\nCRC: split into otp_crc and app_crc columns (the <br> separates them). Row values:\n- 9.5.28: otp \"bdFc\", app \"63b5\"\n- 2.0.30: \"0571\", \"1644\"\n- 2.0.33: \"0571\", \"7e5d\"\n- 2.0.34: \"0571\", \"6D40\"\n- 2.0.35: \"0571\", \"E151\"\n- 2.0.37: \"0571\", \"019A\"\n- 2.0.38: \"0571\", \"6902\"\n- 2.0.40: \"0571\", \"7214\"\n- 2.0.42: \"0571\", \"B459\"\n- 2.0.43: \"0571\", \"2191\"\n- 2.0.44: \"0571\", \"5ab6\"\n- 2.0.46: \"0571\", \"E865\"\n- 2.0.50: \"0571\", \"3cc5\"\n- 2.0.51: \"0571\", \"6b5c\"\n- 2.0.52: \"0571\", \"71ca\"\n- 2.0.53: \"0571\", \"05A2\"\n- 2.0.54: \"0571\", \"1AD3\"\n- 2.0.55: \"0571\", \"48BE\"\n- 2.0.56: \"0571\", \"BFF6\"\n- 2.0.57: \"0571\", \"4C4E\"\n- 2.0.58: \"0571\", \"846C\"\n- 2.0.59: \"0571\", \"078E\"\n- 2.0.60: \"0571\", \"1291\"\n- 2.0.61: \"0571\", \"ECD7\"\n- 2.0.62: \"0571\", \"027C\"\n- 2.0.63: \"0571\", \"736E\"\n- 2.0.65: \"0571\", \"CD67\"\n\nCase preservation: the source has mixed case hex (e.g., \"bdFc\", \"63b5\", \"6D40\", \"E151\", \"019A\", \"6902\", \"7214\", \"B459\", \"2191\", \"5ab6\", \"E865\", \"3cc5\", \"6b5c\", \"71ca\", \"05A2\", \"1AD3\", \"48BE\", \"BFF6\", \"4C4E\", \"846C\", \"078E\", \"1291\", \"ECD7\", \"027C\", \"736E\", \"CD67\"). Preserve exactly as printed.\n\n**revision_history:** dates ISO:\n- \"0\" (Initial), 2021-01-11, changes: null\n- \"1\", 2022-03-17, \"Added production location.\"\n- \"2\", 2023-06-15, \"Extension of line sizes and additional software revisions\"\n- \"3\", 2023-07-04, \"Correction of small error in Q4 flowrate for DN600\"\n- \"4\", 2024-05-17, \"Correction of small error in Q4 flowrate for DN200/DN250\"\n- \"5\", 2025-04-17, \"Addition of the reduced bore version with ratio 400 and software version 2.0.60\"\n- \"6\", 2025-07-31, \"Addition of horizontal housing, IP68 variant and software version 2.0.61\"\n- \"7\", 2025-10-03, \"M5000 Facelift - upgrade of electronics housing and external battery version. Addition software version 2.0.62\"\n- \"8\", 2025-10-03, \"Textual adjustments\"\n- \"9\", 2025-12-23, \"Evaluation of remote mount version and software update\"\n- \"10\", 2026-03-05, \"Manufacturer name change and documentation folder update\"\n- \"11\", 2026-07-28, \"Software update and checksum correc